.TH FMT_ESCAPECHARXML 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
fmt_escapecharxml \- Escape characters for XML format

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/fmt.h>

.IB size_t
.IB fmt_escapecharxml(char* dest, unsigned int ch);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBfmt_escapecharxml\fR function escapes characters for XML format. It takes a destination buffer and a character as arguments. The function escapes the character based on its value according to the rules of XML.

The function takes the following parameters:
.IB char*
A pointer to the destination buffer.
.IB unsigned int
The character to escape.

The function returns the number of bytes written to the destination buffer.

The \fBfmt_escapecharxml\fR function is intended to be used to escape characters for XML format, ensuring that strings can be safely included within XML documents.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBfmt_escapecharxml\fR function to escape characters for XML format:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/fmt.h>

int main() {
    char dest[20];
    unsigned int c = '<';

    size_t written = fmt_escapecharxml(dest, c);

    printf("Written %d bytes: %s\n", written, dest);

    return 0;
}
.nef